quran[21]{c,v,t}:
  54,7,"With their eyes humbled, they will come out of their graves like scattered locusts,"
  54,8,rushing towards the caller. The disbelievers will say: ‘This is a difficult day.’
  54,9,"The people of Nuh (Noah) rejected (the truth) before them. So they denied Our servant and called (him): ‘crazy’, and he was intimidated."
  54,10,"Then he called upon his Lord, saying: ‘Indeed, I have been overcome (by the transgressors), so help (me).’"
  54,11,So We opened the gates of the sky with water pouring down.
  54,12,"And We caused the earth to burst out with springs, and the waters (from all sides) met for a determined matter."
  54,13,"And We carried him (i.e. Noah) upon a thing built with planks and nails (i.e. the Ark),"
  54,14,floating (over the flood waters) under Our eyes. (This was) retribution for the one who was rejected.
  54,15,"Indeed, We have left it as a sign. So is there anyone who will be mindful?"
  54,16,Then how (terrible) were My punishment and My warnings!
  54,17,"Certainly, We have made the Qur’an easy to remember (by simplifying its lessons). So, is there anyone who will be mindful?"
  54,18,(The people of) ‘Ad (also) rejected (their messenger). Then how (terrible) were My punishment and My warnings!
  54,19,"Indeed, We sent upon them a howling tornado on a day of (their) terrible misfortune,"
  54,20,knocking down people as if they were trunks of uprooted palm trees.
  54,21,Then how (terrible) were My punishment and My warnings!
  54,22,"Certainly, We have made the Qur’an easy to remember (by simplifying its lessons). So, is there anyone who will be mindful?"
  54,23,(The people of) Thamud (also) rejected the warnings.
  54,24,"They said: ‘Are we to follow a single human being from among us? Then, we would certainly be in error and madness."
  54,25,"Has the revelation been sent to him (only) from among us? Instead, he is an insolent liar.’"
  54,26,"By tomorrow, they will soon know who the insolent liar is."
  54,27,"We are sending the she-camel as a trial for them. So, watch them (O Salih) and remain patient."
